  "question": {
    "text": "The spin-only magnetic moment value of an octahedral complex among <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NiCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HCl</mi></math>, which upon reaction with excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCl</mi></math> is_____B.M. (Nearest Integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(I) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> no ppt with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CN</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>(II) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>excess</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>CN</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>82</mn><mi>BM</mi><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Aqua complexes, generally have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CN</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>(III) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>Cl</mi><munder><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mover><mi>excess</mi></munder><mn>1</mn></math> Mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>CN</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p>",
